  "$comment": "name-filter.json: the word filter for the scrapyard game's generated names (handles, company names, crew first names). Read by check-words.py beside it. Written 2026-11-25 by the step labelled 'names' (second pass). AN ENGINEER'S FILTER, NOT LEGAL OR MODERATION CLEARANCE. What it catches: (1) a rude word alone, inside a word, or formed where two parts meet ('rudeAnywhere' anywhere in a part or in the joined pair; 'rudeAtJunction' only when a part is exactly that word or the joined pair forms it across the join, because these letters occur inside harmless words: glass, canal, titan); (2) words with an innuendo in this trade (screw, rod, shaft, nut, pipe, tool, drill, plug ...) and 'innuendoAdjectives': size or state words that make one with almost any noun (big, hard, stiff, wet ...) and colour, metal, blood and purity words that make a movement's or a gang's name with one (black, white, iron, storm, pure ...): never used as a part at all; (3) pairs that name a real hate symbol, movement, brand, team or slogan, written out by hand in 'riskyPhrases', plus every list of the fourth game's satire lint (scripts/content/office/deny-*.txt, the same matching: whole words, any case, 'word*' any ending); (4) a part that is a word the specification keeps out of player text ('bannedParts': salvage and haul, yard-design.md 2; group, 7.1); (5) a part or pair equal to, or one letter from, a proper name of the four earlier games (names, titles, characters, places, products; see check-words.py); (6) with --wikidata, every pair in three spellings ('Steady Anvil', 'Steady anvil', 'Steadyanvil') looked up as an exact English Wikipedia title through Wikidata: a page of that title means a real thing of that name (a place, brand, team, band, film, song, species), and the pair is flagged. Remove words until nothing is flagged; never add an 'allow' list to let a flagged pair through.",
